# "Return this card to the battlefield transformed" (CR 702.167a): a token copy of Dire Flail (Three Steps Ahead's copy
# mode) has the craft ability and may activate it, but the token exiled to pay the cost ceases to exist (CR 111.7,
# 704.5d), so as the ability resolves there is no card to return and nothing enters. The real Dire Flail, an artifact
# Bot1 controls other than the token, is the material: exiled, and not returned either - only "this card" is.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Dire Flail
Three Steps Ahead
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dire Flail.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Three Steps Ahead.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Dire Flail)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dire Flail#2.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Dire Flail#2.Activate(Ability: Craft)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Choose(craft materials)
Bot1.Choose(Dire Flail)
? Exile = Dire Flail

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Island; Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby
Exile = Dire Flail
Stack.Count = 0
